WEBVTT

00:01.890 --> 00:05.770
<i>This world is filled with 
too many games to count,</i>

00:06.980 --> 00:11.240
<i>though the vast majority simply 
come and go in obscurity.</i>

00:12.540 --> 00:15.380
<i>The greatest of all games</i>

00:15.380 --> 00:20.680
<i>is the fully immersive VR game boasting 
over 30 million players worldwide—</i>

00:20.680 --> 00:25.310
<i></i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>, which rightly 
earns the title of "god-tier game"!</i>

00:27.000 --> 00:30.910
<i>One lover of trash games, Rakuro Hizutome,</i>

00:30.910 --> 00:34.100
<i>is trying out the god-tier 
game, </i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i>

00:34.930 --> 00:39.650
<i>What adventures await him there?</i>

02:18.190 --> 02:21.990
Okay, let's get climbing!

02:22.340 --> 02:27.250
<b>Rare Items, Worth More Than Life Itself</b>

02:23.170 --> 02:26.930
Wait for me, Crystal Scorpions!

02:28.060 --> 02:31.980
First, I'll use Moon Jumper to 
boost my vertical jumping power.

02:32.100 --> 02:32.290
Moon Jumper

02:32.700 --> 02:34.750
Then... Six-Boat Leap!

02:42.390 --> 02:46.050
Over-level-100 monsters, 
the Crystal Scorpions...

02:46.360 --> 02:48.570
I gotta find out what they are!

02:48.570 --> 02:52.140
It'd be pretty rude not to 
say hi while I'm in the area!

02:52.450 --> 02:55.670
What, you expect me to find out about an 
unexplored area filled with unknown monsters

02:55.670 --> 02:57.690
and just forget about it?!

02:57.690 --> 03:00.470
What's the point of playing games 
if you can't go buck wild?!

03:13.230 --> 03:16.210
Hey, would you look at that?

03:16.540 --> 03:20.500
It's way more fantastical 
than the area down below...

03:20.740 --> 03:24.740
<b>Crystal Nest Cliff</b>

03:26.220 --> 03:28.570
Really hard to make progress...

03:28.570 --> 03:31.230
The footing's just terrible.

03:31.690 --> 03:37.730
Okay, let's find those Crystal 
Scorpions I've heard so much a—

03:47.650 --> 03:49.620
So they're the type to camouflage 
into the field, huh?

03:50.550 --> 03:53.620
You're the one I'm here 
to see, Crystal Scorpion!

03:53.620 --> 03:56.090
<b>Crystal Scorpion</b>

03:59.190 --> 04:00.170
Too damn close!

04:10.180 --> 04:12.270
This thing's like a runaway train!

04:12.270 --> 04:14.660
Guess it utilizes the field's awful footing

04:14.660 --> 04:17.940
to drive the players into a dead end, huh?

04:21.150 --> 04:22.460
Well, what's the matter?

04:22.460 --> 04:24.740
Is a straight-up charge 
the only trick you know?

04:27.200 --> 04:29.540
My first time around, 
I'm just here to say hi.

04:29.540 --> 04:32.540
I don't expect to beat the 
thing in my current state.

04:33.910 --> 04:37.550
Scout out the area, take back 
any rare materials I find—

04:37.550 --> 04:39.420
That's my mission today!

04:42.670 --> 04:45.420
If I can do that, I'll take it as a win...

04:48.450 --> 04:49.190
Huh?

04:57.460 --> 05:01.570
<b>Crystal Scorpions</b>

05:03.820 --> 05:06.790
They're a bunch of tough 
nuts not even I could crack.

05:06.790 --> 05:09.450
Crystal Scorpions attack as a swarm,

05:09.450 --> 05:11.450
so if one sees you, you're dead.

05:24.690 --> 05:26.010
<i>Yeah...</i>

05:26.990 --> 05:28.800
<i>Okay, I'm dead.</i>

05:37.780 --> 05:41.360
I wonder when Sunraku-san 
might finally return...

05:41.360 --> 05:47.080
Oh, what if he's unable 
to return to Rabituza?!

05:47.080 --> 05:51.130
Perhaps I should have waited for 
him in Eighthold after all?!

05:49.340 --> 05:52.550
<b>Respawn
Rabituza</b>

05:51.130 --> 05:52.870
Freaking damn it!

05:52.870 --> 05:56.500
That's too many of those 
stupid scorpion jerks!

05:57.080 --> 05:58.530
Hey, Emul!

05:58.530 --> 05:59.920
Can I get a gate back to Eighthold?

06:00.980 --> 06:02.590
Sunraku-san...

06:02.940 --> 06:06.540
You <i>have</i> been fighting the 
Crystal Scorpions, haven't you?!

06:06.540 --> 06:07.720
Ah, crud.

06:07.720 --> 06:11.330
We told you the 
Crystal Scorpions were dangerous!

06:11.330 --> 06:12.350
Man, this sucks.

06:12.350 --> 06:14.180
What did you just say?!

06:14.500 --> 06:17.370
Here you are! The carrot I promised you!

06:17.370 --> 06:18.850
Hooray!

06:22.180 --> 06:24.840
Truly delicious!

06:24.840 --> 06:28.200
You're so predictable, it's kind of scary.

06:40.390 --> 06:44.050
Okay, I'm gonna give it another go.

06:44.050 --> 06:46.210
Really, must you go?

06:46.210 --> 06:49.630
I can't hang it up until 
I get something out of it.

06:49.630 --> 06:51.720
And this won't be my first visit.

06:52.390 --> 06:54.270
I won't die empty-handed.

07:03.810 --> 07:07.710
Okay... let's move slow and keep hidden.

07:09.100 --> 07:12.920
I noticed a pretty interesting spot last time.

07:17.300 --> 07:19.260
Hey, there it is.

07:26.710 --> 07:29.760
I got a glimpse at it 
just before they got me.

07:30.420 --> 07:35.760
A shiny li'l number that's 
just begging for my pickax.

07:38.930 --> 07:42.980
I bet it gives up items unique to this area!

08:06.500 --> 08:09.930
Damn it! I'm not giving up!

08:11.280 --> 08:12.470
<b>Overheat
 Climax Boost
 Nitro Gain</b>

08:16.840 --> 08:20.150
I'm gonna get me some loot, no matter what!

08:29.940 --> 08:33.280
That one went by fast.

08:35.990 --> 08:37.090
It's no use.

08:37.530 --> 08:39.220
They're so big, and so fast...

08:39.660 --> 08:43.290
And they overwhelm you with numbers in an 
area that's already hard to maneuver in.

08:43.730 --> 08:45.670
How am I supposed to survive that?

08:45.670 --> 08:48.660
It's just as we told you, yes!

08:48.980 --> 08:52.970
Yeah... but I also told <i>you</i> something, Emul.

08:54.470 --> 08:57.190
I won't die empty-handed.

08:59.420 --> 09:00.740
Let's have a look.

09:00.740 --> 09:01.520
Let's have a look!

09:01.520 --> 09:19.530
<b>Aroncaleth Hard Lapis
Produced via repeated compression and
refinement through ingestion by
geophagic monsters, refinement through ingestion 
by geophagic monsters, its beautiful blue color 
recalls the land itself.</b>

09:02.390 --> 09:04.570
"Aroncaleth Hard Lapis"

09:04.900 --> 09:06.660
"Produced via repeated compression and

09:06.660 --> 09:10.850
refinement through ingestion 
by geophagic monsters,

09:10.850 --> 09:14.230
this crystal possesses an 
extremely dense magic content.

09:14.750 --> 09:18.590
Its beautiful blue color 
recalls the land itself."

09:19.880 --> 09:21.940
I dunno what I'd use it for,

09:21.940 --> 09:24.230
but it's gotta be worth more 
than what I spent to get it.

09:24.230 --> 09:26.470
I'm gonna check the game guide site later!

09:26.470 --> 09:28.040
Are you satisfied now?

09:28.370 --> 09:29.890
Maybe.

09:29.890 --> 09:34.270
I hate to give up here, but I should 
probably take a break for the day.

09:37.110 --> 09:39.050
Yes, you should have a nice sleep!

09:40.520 --> 09:42.830
<i>The Crystal Scorpions...</i>

09:43.230 --> 09:47.960
<i>The slightest vibration on the 
crystals gets them swarming you.</i>

09:47.960 --> 09:50.690
<i>Though the AI's not particularly clever...</i>

09:50.690 --> 09:55.200
Go to sleep, go to sleep,

09:55.200 --> 09:58.820
<i>They just charge at me mindlessly, so...</i>

09:55.200 --> 09:59.200
beneath your bunny's ears...

09:59.780 --> 10:05.250
<i>When they collided, they tore 
off each other's carapace...</i>

10:06.750 --> 10:08.870
Hang on a freaking minute here!

10:08.870 --> 10:12.500
Could I get the torn-off 
carapace bits as an item?!

10:12.860 --> 10:14.980
Man, I wanna find out!

10:14.980 --> 10:17.760
Now that I got the idea, I wanna find out!

10:18.140 --> 10:19.970
Emul, open the gate!

10:19.970 --> 10:20.970
I'm going back!

10:20.970 --> 10:24.290
What? You still haven't given up?

10:24.290 --> 10:25.770
They're just going to kill you again!

10:25.770 --> 10:32.650
<b>I want materials</b>

10:26.070 --> 10:30.120
As long as there's unknowns out there, 
a pioneer must never fear death!

10:30.120 --> 10:32.650
You're clearly fueled by greed.

10:33.530 --> 10:39.740
But... even if I <i>could</i> pick it up, 
how would I go about doing it?

10:40.520 --> 10:45.430
It was pretty much luck that 
let me recover that mineral...

10:45.930 --> 10:47.370
Honestly.

10:49.870 --> 10:52.910
The mana used to open gates 
isn't free, you know!

10:55.380 --> 10:57.670
That's it!

10:58.380 --> 11:00.880
You just gave me a great idea, Emul!

11:00.880 --> 11:03.100
That'll work just fine!

11:03.100 --> 11:06.600
Wh-What are you going to do?!

11:08.670 --> 11:10.070
Just you wait!

11:10.070 --> 11:11.400
I'm gonna take that Crystal Scorpion

11:11.400 --> 11:13.800
minefield swarming with 
level-100-plus monsters...

11:13.800 --> 11:16.610
and turn it into a walk in the park!

11:17.500 --> 11:21.260
Please put me down now!

11:33.130 --> 11:36.250
What's wrong, buddy? I'm right here!

11:38.270 --> 11:40.010
So scary!

11:49.300 --> 11:51.990
Oh, gosh, I'm surrounded!

11:51.990 --> 11:55.520
What do I do? I'm in so much trouble!

12:01.500 --> 12:03.030
Just kidding.

12:03.380 --> 12:04.030
<b>Six-Boat Leap</b>

12:03.720 --> 12:05.380
Six-Boat Leap!

12:11.190 --> 12:12.540
Okay, great!

12:12.970 --> 12:15.040
Carapace breakage confirmed!

12:19.050 --> 12:22.150
You wanna run me through 
the scorpion blender, huh?

12:22.150 --> 12:25.220
Part of me would like to find 
out what that feels like,

12:25.220 --> 12:29.140
but it might be kinda traumatic, 
so I'll pass this time.

12:30.290 --> 12:31.940
Enter Travel!

12:30.290 --> 12:33.730
<b>Enter Travel</b>

12:43.450 --> 12:44.340
<b>{missing}</b>

12:43.450 --> 12:44.340
<b>{Missing} {Z: I couldn't find this in the masref}</b>

12:49.160 --> 12:52.150
Three cheers for civilization! Inventoria!

12:50.180 --> 12:52.410
<b>Inventoria</b>

12:52.150 --> 12:55.300
Technology always gets the last laugh!

12:58.390 --> 13:01.740
<i>I got the idea from watching 
Emul use that item.</i>

13:01.740 --> 13:07.050
<i>I can move myself instantly to the Inventoria, 
like I'd transmit an item or a weapon.</i>

13:07.050 --> 13:10.430
<i>That means I can create myself 
a safe space wherever I need it!</i>

13:11.210 --> 13:16.610
This Inventoria thing is seriously 
OP if you use it right!

13:17.670 --> 13:21.380
Now... guess it's time to head back.

13:22.500 --> 13:24.120
Exit Travel!

13:22.500 --> 13:25.700
<b>Exit Travel</b>

13:33.700 --> 13:34.960
<b>Dropped Item
Crystal Leg</b>

13:34.960 --> 13:36.210
<b>Dropped Item
Crystal Scorpion's Carapace</b>

13:36.210 --> 13:37.460
<b>Dropped Item
Crystal Pincer</b>

13:37.460 --> 13:38.710
<b>Dropped Item
Crystal Talon</b>

13:41.710 --> 13:43.440
Hell yeah!

13:43.440 --> 13:47.380
Just like I thought, 
the Crystal Scorpions cleared out!

13:47.380 --> 13:50.300
Time to loot all the spoils!

13:55.960 --> 14:00.310
Materials from monsters that 
tough have gotta be pretty rare!

14:00.310 --> 14:03.360
Bet you Bilac could make 
something awesome out of them!

14:03.360 --> 14:06.250
I'm so awesome! I'm a genius!

14:19.650 --> 14:22.230
I'm gonna make materials 
out of every one of you!

14:22.230 --> 14:25.510
Come at me in the tens or the hundreds!

14:28.540 --> 14:32.840
Just you wait, Bilac! 
I'm gonna have a huge collection for you!

14:37.370 --> 14:40.330
Players have a hard limit 
on inventory capacity.

14:37.900 --> 14:44.300
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!{bg}

14:40.330 --> 14:44.300
If you carry too much, it gets 
too heavy, and slows you down.

14:44.650 --> 14:45.560
But...

14:45.530 --> 14:50.030
<b>Inventoria Key</b>

14:46.100 --> 14:52.190
The Inventoria lets you store unlimited 
objects with no penalty at all!

14:49.700 --> 14:52.530
Yay! Yay! Unlimited!{bg}

14:52.530 --> 14:55.040
Inventoria Key

14:52.960 --> 14:55.040
So if you use it just right...

15:01.920 --> 15:07.740
I can get unlimited materials from 
the over-level-100 Crystal Scorpions!

15:07.740 --> 15:09.930
You rock, Inventoria!

15:10.310 --> 15:15.430
I just hide out in the Inventoria until 
the Crystal Scorpions' aggro dies down...

15:17.800 --> 15:22.330
Then I return to the real world when the 
heat's off, and would you look at that?

15:22.730 --> 15:26.730
The Crystal Scorpions are gone, 
back to hiding in the scenery,

15:26.730 --> 15:27.980
<b>Dropped Item
Crystal Leg</b>

15:26.990 --> 15:31.740
and the ground is littered with items 
generated from their infighting!

15:27.980 --> 15:29.240
<b>Dropped Item
Crystal Scorpion's Carapace</b>

15:29.240 --> 15:30.490
<b>Dropped Item
Crystal Pincer</b>

15:30.490 --> 15:31.740
<b>Dropped Item
Crystal Talon</b>

15:32.120 --> 15:35.320
Figuring out these little tricks 
is what I love about gaming!

15:35.320 --> 15:38.240
I'm gonna get so many valuable materials!

15:38.950 --> 15:40.340
Although...

15:40.520 --> 15:47.500
Sunraku

15:40.670 --> 15:43.510
Looks like I'm pretty low on MP.

15:43.510 --> 15:47.500
I'm down to my last use of the Inventoria.

15:47.870 --> 15:51.610
But I still got tons of sweet item drops!

15:51.610 --> 15:54.010
I'll do one last run, then head back.

15:54.010 --> 16:00.020
<b>Crystal Leg
 Crystal Talon
 Crystal Pincer
 Crystal Scorpion's Carapace
 Aroncaleth Hard Lapis
Lapisteria Stellar Crystal
 Amurcidian Quartz
 Crystalline Sand
 Lowenanva Amber Crystal</b>

15:55.010 --> 16:00.020
Still, there's something so satisfying 
just looking through rare items...

16:01.240 --> 16:03.110
Eh? What's this?

16:03.490 --> 16:05.150
Wait a minute!

16:05.620 --> 16:07.770
I still don't have a stinger?

16:08.390 --> 16:12.650
You can't fight a scorpion and 
not get a stinger, can you?

16:12.650 --> 16:14.910
It's kind of the most defining feature!

16:15.870 --> 16:21.410
Maybe the stinger's too sturdy to 
tear off just from basic infighting?

16:22.280 --> 16:25.420
Seems pretty plausible, which means...

16:25.770 --> 16:30.170
The Crystal Scorpion's stinger 
could be the rare drop!

16:30.590 --> 16:32.150
Okay, I get it.

16:32.150 --> 16:34.870
I definitely wanna get me one of those.

16:35.230 --> 16:36.280
But...

16:36.890 --> 16:39.160
In order to get that rare drop,

16:39.160 --> 16:41.960
I'm gonna have to face a horde 
of level-100-plus monsters,

16:41.960 --> 16:45.940
in a place with awful footing, 
and pinpoint target the stinger.

16:47.590 --> 16:55.100
And the part I'm after is so super-tough 
that normal attacks won't break it off.

17:06.510 --> 17:07.880
C'mon, guys.

17:07.880 --> 17:10.960
This is some trash game-tier stuff, y'know?

17:13.750 --> 17:16.300
But that's what's gonna make it fun!

17:16.660 --> 17:18.260
Let's get it done!

17:19.030 --> 17:23.210
I'm gonna tear off your precious 
stinger, no matter what it takes!

17:23.210 --> 17:25.690
On my honor as a trash gamer!

17:30.750 --> 17:31.440
<b>Overheat
 Climax Boost
 Nitro Gain</b>

17:39.260 --> 17:41.430
Even with my buff stack, it's a no-go?!

17:41.430 --> 17:43.620
Figures it'd be that tough!

17:43.620 --> 17:45.210
Didn't even leave a crack!

17:50.740 --> 17:54.410
<i>I had a feeling I might 
need some help on this.</i>

17:56.840 --> 18:01.290
<i>I'll have to get their attacks 
to focus on a single stinger!</i>

18:02.750 --> 18:05.940
<i>I can't fully control my enemies' attacks.</i>

18:06.660 --> 18:10.860
<i>Getting the best possible pull out 
of the random number generator...</i>

18:11.490 --> 18:14.110
<i>That's what being a gamer is about!</i>

18:18.030 --> 18:20.030
<i>Dodge the stingers' attacks.</i>

18:20.030 --> 18:20.990
<i>Land.</i>

18:23.190 --> 18:26.510
<i>Stay to the very last second to 
lure the other scorpions' attack...</i>

18:27.490 --> 18:29.920
<i>Yes, that could do it!</i>

18:30.440 --> 18:32.920
<i>I only get one chance at this.</i>

18:33.920 --> 18:35.920
Enter Travel!

18:41.720 --> 18:44.430
Then right back to reality!

18:48.050 --> 18:50.100
Perfect placement!

18:50.490 --> 18:53.110
You rock, Goddess of RNG!

18:53.460 --> 18:55.110
<b>Overheat
 Climax Boost
 Nitro Gain</b>

18:53.580 --> 18:56.530
Now that the stinger's pretty busted...

18:55.110 --> 18:56.590
<b>Overheat
 Climax Boost
 Nitro Gain</b>

18:56.860 --> 18:59.360
Glowing Pierce

18:56.860 --> 18:59.360
Glowing Pierce

18:57.020 --> 18:59.390
Glowing Pierce!

19:03.400 --> 19:06.040
Just break already!

19:09.240 --> 19:11.580
Yeah! How you like that?!

19:11.860 --> 19:15.090
That's what I can do when 
I put my mind to it!

19:15.650 --> 19:18.580
Got me a rare drop!

19:18.910 --> 19:21.310
<i>The second I claim it,</i>

19:21.310 --> 19:24.600
<i>even if I'm insta-killed, 
I'll still get to keep the...</i>

19:25.590 --> 19:27.570
<i>Hey. Hang on.</i>

19:27.570 --> 19:28.600
<i>Huh?</i>

19:28.810 --> 19:31.550
<i>I'm not as close as I thought I was.</i>

19:32.460 --> 19:34.760
<i>Huh? You're kidding me, right?</i>

19:34.760 --> 19:35.860
<i>I almost had it.</i>

19:36.390 --> 19:39.360
<i>If my trajectory had been 
just a little different,</i>

19:39.880 --> 19:41.100
<i>I could've had it.</i>

19:42.850 --> 19:48.120
<i>Hey, you listening? Goddess of RNG?</i>

19:48.120 --> 19:53.150
<i>Why you gotta be so cruel?</i>

19:59.050 --> 20:02.930
A-Are you all right, Sunraku-san?!

20:06.740 --> 20:11.400
You haven't moved this whole time, 
and you seem to be trembling...

20:12.590 --> 20:13.370
Yeah...

20:13.880 --> 20:18.190
I can break off the scorpion's stinger, 
and it's possible to retrieve it.

20:18.790 --> 20:22.950
I know that now, so... I guess that's enough.

20:23.620 --> 20:24.980
It's enough. Yeah, it is.

20:28.170 --> 20:30.670
Like hell it is!

20:30.670 --> 20:33.510
It doesn't mean jack if 
I don't get the thing!

20:34.960 --> 20:43.340
<b>Random Number
Generator</b>

20:35.510 --> 20:39.310
Screw you, Goddess of RNG! You totally suck!

20:39.310 --> 20:43.340
Missing it when you almost had it is the 
biggest psychological blow you can take!

20:43.340 --> 20:46.250
And despite getting stuck 
in the scorpion blender,

20:46.250 --> 20:49.350
why didn't it tear up the Staring Bird Mask?!

20:49.350 --> 20:53.060
Was it a miracle? Why is <i>that </i>
where I pull the miracle RNG?!

20:53.060 --> 20:56.480
It actually kinda makes me more pissed!

20:57.070 --> 21:00.980
Sunraku-san has grown rather unstable.

21:03.820 --> 21:05.860
That pissed me off way too much.

21:05.860 --> 21:09.450
I don't wanna look at any 
more scorpions for a while.

21:15.330 --> 21:19.460
There's only one way to 
bounce back from this.

21:20.220 --> 21:21.960
Wh-What is is?

21:22.380 --> 21:24.440
I'm gonna brag to Bilac 
about the materials I got

21:24.440 --> 21:26.540
and bathe in her praise!

21:27.330 --> 21:32.200
I just know she'll appreciate how 
valuable these materials are!

21:32.200 --> 21:34.480
Time is money! Let's go, Emul!

21:34.980 --> 21:38.230
R-Righty-o...

21:38.230 --> 21:43.450
Nothing beats the moment when you brag 
to someone about your accomplishments!

21:43.450 --> 21:45.970
That's rather perverse thinking!

21:45.970 --> 21:49.400
Sorry, but I take that as a compliment!

23:24.630 --> 23:28.140
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

23:24.630 --> 23:31.220
<b>SLF Mini</b>

23:27.720 --> 23:31.220
<i><b>Records of Battles With Lycagon</b></i>

23:28.640 --> 23:30.650
Mini!

23:31.220 --> 23:32.220
<b>Equip</b>

23:31.220 --> 25:57.360
<i><b>SLF Theater</b></i>

23:32.240 --> 23:33.590
<b>Cannot equip.</b>

23:33.610 --> 23:34.970
<b>Cannot equip.</b>

23:34.990 --> 23:35.970
<b>Cannot equip.</b>

23:35.990 --> 23:36.350
<b>Cannot equip.</b>

23:36.370 --> 23:36.760
<b>Cannot equip.</b>

23:36.780 --> 23:36.970
<b>Cannot equip.</b>

23:37.380 --> 23:39.550
Curse you, Lycagon!

23:40.510 --> 23:43.740
What now? Still wasting your time on that?

23:43.740 --> 23:46.040
There could be a glitch that gives a

23:46.040 --> 23:50.040
fraction-of-a-percent chance of breaking 
through Lycagon's curse to put on armor.

23:50.040 --> 23:52.520
Well, dreaming is free.

23:52.520 --> 23:54.540
Everything past that will cost you.

23:54.540 --> 23:56.370
So stingy!

23:56.370 --> 24:00.890
Speaking of, quite a few people 
have fought Lycagon, right?

24:00.890 --> 24:02.750
It's just that no one's beaten it.

24:05.290 --> 24:07.560
Yeah, that's true.

24:07.560 --> 24:08.600
Momo-cha—

24:08.600 --> 24:11.740
Someone I know is pretty passionate about it.

24:11.740 --> 24:13.450
But they haven't beaten it?

24:13.450 --> 24:15.870
Just don't mention that her.

24:15.870 --> 24:17.050
I have, of course.

24:17.050 --> 24:18.150
You...

24:20.520 --> 24:25.110
So, just for my edification, 
how did this person fight it?

24:25.110 --> 24:28.550
Well, from what I've heard,

24:28.550 --> 24:31.030
they came at it with a V formation,

24:31.030 --> 24:34.950
but it got behind them and blew 
them away like bowling pins.

24:38.710 --> 24:43.450
Then they tried the Dynamite 
Bone-in Muscle Burst.

24:43.450 --> 24:48.090
Momo-chan said that one 
went pretty well, I think.

24:48.650 --> 24:49.650
The what?

24:49.650 --> 24:52.000
Oh, would you look at the time?

24:52.000 --> 24:55.260
Sorry, I've got an early 
morning. Better log out.

24:55.260 --> 24:56.470
Hey! Wait a minute!

24:56.470 --> 24:57.850
You can't just not explain that one!

24:59.160 --> 25:02.630
Dynamite Bone-in Muscle Burst?

25:04.340 --> 25:07.860
Dynamite Bone-in Muscle Burst?

25:09.260 --> 25:12.520
Dynamite Bone-in Muscle Burst?

25:16.220 --> 25:20.120
S-Sunraku-san, what are you doing?

25:26.870 --> 25:29.420
Bone-in meat and a muscle burst!

25:29.420 --> 25:32.260
Bone-in meat and a muscle burst?!

25:33.300 --> 25:35.790
So I just need the dynamite.

25:36.570 --> 25:38.370
An explosion.

25:38.900 --> 25:41.340
That's where you come in, Emul.

25:41.700 --> 25:45.250
Wh-What are you going to get me to do?

25:45.250 --> 25:48.400
Explosion? Are you going to explode me?!

25:48.400 --> 25:52.020
You're going to become the dynamite!

25:52.810 --> 25:56.680
No!
